1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,168
有个问题，听起来很简单
Here's a question that sounds easy.

2
00:00:02,488 --> 00:00:05,131
井字棋有多少种不同的对局？
How many different games of tic-tac-toe are there?

3
00:00:05,367 --> 00:00:09,180
这里说的“一局”，指的是从第一步到最后一步
By a game, we mean the whole list of moves,

4
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:11,168
按顺序排好的全部走法
in order.

5
00:00:11,488 --> 00:00:14,400
所以，如果两局最后的棋盘一样
So if two games end with the same board,

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,865
但走棋的顺序不同，那它们要算作两种不同的对局
but the moves happened in a different order, they count as two different games.

7
00:00:19,185 --> 00:00:23,028
棋盘翻转或旋转后得到的对局，也分开算
Flipped or turned versions count separately too.

8
00:00:24,067 --> 00:00:25,814
猜一猜。一百？
Take a guess. A hundred?

9
00:00:26,134 --> 00:00:30,017
一百万？暂停一下视频，把你猜的数写下来
A million? Pause the video and write your guess down.

10
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:41,000
答案是 255,168
The answer is 255,168.

11
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:45,591
在这个视频里，我们会弄清楚这个数字是怎么来的
In this video we'll find out where that number comes from: first by careful counting,

12
00:00:45,591 --> 00:00:50,604
先仔细地算，再用一段短短的电脑程序，把每一局都下一遍
and then with a short computer program that plays every single game.

13
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:53,552
先看一个更简单的问题
Let's start with a simpler question.

14
00:00:53,872 --> 00:00:56,175
假设有人三子连成一线了
Suppose the players ignore three in a row,

15
00:00:56,175 --> 00:00:59,630
双方也不停，一直下到九个格子都填满
and just keep going until all nine squares are full.

16
00:00:59,950 --> 00:01:02,748
填满棋盘有多少种不同的顺序？
In how many different orders can the board fill up?

17
00:01:02,983 --> 00:01:05,559
X 先走，有 9 个格子可以选
X goes first and has 9 squares to choose from.

18
00:01:05,879 --> 00:01:09,047
不管 X 下在哪儿，O 都还剩 8 个格子
For each of those, O has 8 squares left.

19
00:01:09,367 --> 00:01:12,576
这就是 9 个 8，所以选择数要相乘
That's 9 groups of 8, so the choices multiply:

20
00:01:12,576 --> 00:01:16,905
9 乘 8 等于 72，前两步就有 72 种不同的下法
9 times 8 is 72 different ways to make the first two moves.

21
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:21,953
继续乘下去：9 乘 8 乘 7，依此类推，一直乘到 1
Keep going: 9 times 8 times 7, and so on, all the way down to 1.

22
00:01:22,273 --> 00:01:24,944
数学家给这种连乘起了个名字
Mathematicians have a short name for this:

23
00:01:24,944 --> 00:01:28,330
9 的阶乘，写成 9 后面加一个感叹号
nine factorial, written as a 9 with an exclamation mark.

24
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:31,269
它等于 362,880
It equals 362,880.

25
00:01:31,517 --> 00:01:33,097
可是，等一下
But wait.

26
00:01:33,147 --> 00:01:36,115
这比 255,168 还要多
That's more than 255,168.

27
00:01:36,435 --> 00:01:38,058
我们算出来的太多了
Our count is too high.

28
00:01:38,378 --> 00:01:41,112
这些多出来的对局，都是从哪儿来的？
Where are all those extra games coming from?

29
00:01:42,750 --> 00:01:48,516
问题就在这儿。真正的井字棋，一有人三子连成一线，就结束了
Here's the catch. Real tic-tac-toe stops as soon as someone gets three in a row.

30
00:01:48,836 --> 00:01:54,542
这一局，X 在第 5 步就赢了，所以剩下的四个格子从没下过
In this game, X wins on the fifth move, so the last four squares are never played.

31
00:01:54,783 --> 00:01:59,557
可是 362,880 还是把这几步没下的棋也算进去了
But our 362,880 counted those missing moves anyway,

32
00:01:59,557 --> 00:02:02,886
就好像赢了以后，双方还在接着下
as if the players kept going after the win.

33
00:02:03,206 --> 00:02:06,839
填满这 4 个空格子，有 4 乘 3 乘 2 乘 1
The 4 empty squares can be filled in 4 times 3 times 2 times 1,

34
00:02:06,839 --> 00:02:08,980
也就是 24 种不同的顺序
so 24 ways.

35
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:11,746
所以这一局被算了 24 次！
So this one game got counted 24 times!

36
00:02:12,066 --> 00:02:15,253
我们把这些编出来的对局叫作“幽灵对局”
Let's call those made-up endings ghost games.

37
00:02:15,573 --> 00:02:18,664
我们要让每一局真实的对局都只算一次
We want to count each real game only once.

38
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:20,930
一局最早什么时候能结束？
So when can a game end?

39
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:22,850
至少要到第 5 步
Not before move 5.

40
00:02:23,005 --> 00:02:27,372
X 下的是第 1、3、5 步，所以到了第 5 步
X plays moves 1, 3 and 5, so the fifth move is the first

41
00:02:27,372 --> 00:02:29,929
才可能有人凑齐三个棋子
time anyone can have three marks.

42
00:02:30,167 --> 00:02:34,906
暂停想一想：有多少种对局是 X 在第 5 步赢下的？
Pause and ponder: how many games end with X winning on move 5?

43
00:02:35,226 --> 00:02:37,488
先自己算一算，再看答案
Try to count them before I show you.

44
00:02:57,733 --> 00:02:59,908
这里有个办法，分三个步骤
Here's one way, in three steps.

45
00:03:00,228 --> 00:03:03,091
第一，选出 X 获胜的那条线
First, pick the line X wins with.

46
00:03:03,411 --> 00:03:07,273
一共有 8 条：3 排、3 列和 2 条对角线
There are 8: 3 rows, 3 columns and 2 diagonals.

47
00:03:07,593 --> 00:03:11,213
第二，X 可以按不同的顺序填满这条线
Second, X fills that line in some order:

48
00:03:11,213 --> 00:03:16,044
3 乘 2 乘 1，也就是 3 的阶乘，所以有 6 种顺序
3 times 2 times 1, which is 3 factorial, so 6 orders.

49
00:03:16,364 --> 00:03:19,792
第三，第一个 O 有另外 6 个格子可以选
Third, O's first mark can go on any of the other 6 squares,

50
00:03:19,792 --> 00:03:24,633
第二个 O 还剩 5 个格子可以选：6 乘 5 等于 30 种放法
and O's second mark on any of the 5 left: 6 times 5 is 30 ways.

51
00:03:24,953 --> 00:03:29,745
把它们乘起来：8 乘 6 乘 30 等于 1,440 种对局
Multiply: 8 times 6 times 30 is 1,440 games.

52
00:03:31,583 --> 00:03:33,746
那 O 在第 6 步赢下的对局呢？
What about games that O wins on move 6?

53
00:03:34,066 --> 00:03:35,871
O 需要三子连成一线
O needs three in a row.

54
00:03:36,191 --> 00:03:39,617
但要小心：如果三个 X 也连成了一线
But careful: if X's three marks also make a line,

55
00:03:39,617 --> 00:03:44,935
X 在第 5 步就已经赢了，还没等 O 连完，这一局就结束了
X already won on move 5, and the game stopped before O could finish.

56
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:48,717
还是用那三个步骤：O 有 8 条线可选
Use the same three steps: 8 lines for O,

57
00:03:48,717 --> 00:03:54,360
O 填满这条线有 6 种顺序，三个 X 有 6 乘 5 乘 4 种放法
6 orders for O's marks, and 6 times 5 times 4 ways to place X's three marks.

58
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:58,880
这样，O 一共有 5,760 种方法连成一线
That's 5,760 ways for O to finish a line.

59
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:04,241
然后再减去 432 种情况：三个 X 也连成了一线
Then we subtract the 432 where X's three marks made a line too,

60
00:04:04,241 --> 00:04:10,159
正好是和 O 那条线平行的一排或一列，所以 X 抢先赢了
a row or column parallel to O's, so X sneaked in a win first.

61
00:04:10,479 --> 00:04:13,444
最后剩下 5,328 种对局
That leaves 5,328 games.

62
00:04:13,683 --> 00:04:17,403
在第 7、8、9 步结束的对局就麻烦多了
For games that end on moves 7, 8 and 9,

63
00:04:17,403 --> 00:04:20,975
我们必须检查之前的每一步有没有人赢
it gets much worse: we'd have to check every earlier move for a win,

64
00:04:20,975 --> 00:04:25,141
而且下满的棋盘可能是有人赢，也可能是平局
and a full board might be a win or a draw.

65
00:04:25,461 --> 00:04:27,175
这就变成了一团乱麻
It turns into a tangled mess.

66
00:04:27,416 --> 00:04:30,833
手算变得这么乱的时候，我们还有 Plan B
When counting gets this messy, there's another plan.

67
00:04:31,153 --> 00:04:32,730
别再想巧办法了
Don't count cleverly.

68
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:36,238
不如教电脑学会规则，再让它一局接一局
Instead, teach a computer the rules,

69
00:04:36,238 --> 00:04:38,604
把所有可能的对局都下一遍
and let it play every possible game, one by one.

70
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:42,042
首先，电脑需要一个棋盘
First, the computer needs a board.

71
00:04:42,362 --> 00:04:44,816
我们用一个列表来存 9 个格子
We'll use a list of 9 squares.

72
00:04:45,136 --> 00:04:49,012
我们用的编程语言叫 Python；在 Python 里
In Python, the programming language we're using,

73
00:04:49,012 --> 00:04:53,709
列表里的位置从零开始编号，所以格子的编号是 0 到 8
the spots in a list are numbered starting from zero, so our squares are numbered 0 to 8.

74
00:04:54,029 --> 00:04:55,629
空格子里放一个点
An empty square holds a dot.

75
00:04:57,017 --> 00:04:59,948
接下来，电脑要知道怎样才算赢
Next, the computer needs to know what counts as a win.

76
00:05:00,268 --> 00:05:03,183
我们直接把所有能赢的线都列出来
We simply list all 8 winning lines,

77
00:05:03,183 --> 00:05:06,762
一共 8 条，每条线写成一组三个格子编号
as groups of three square numbers.

78
00:05:07,082 --> 00:05:10,599
0、1、2 号格组成最上面一排
Squares 0, 1 and 2 make the top row.

79
00:05:10,919 --> 00:05:14,375
0、4、8 号格组成一条对角线
Squares 0, 4 and 8 make a diagonal.

80
00:05:15,317 --> 00:05:20,499
接下来是一个函数：在编程里，函数就是一小段有名字的程序
Next comes a function: a little mini-program with a name.

81
00:05:20,819 --> 00:05:25,635
这个函数叫 winner，意思是“赢家”，它会检查每一条线
This one, called winner, checks every line.

82
00:05:25,955 --> 00:05:28,755
如果一条线上三个格子放的都一样
If all three squares on a line hold the same mark,

83
00:05:28,755 --> 00:05:32,080
而且不是点，那这是谁的棋子，谁就赢了
and that mark isn't a dot, that player has won.

84
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:36,112
如果没有一条线符合，winner 什么也没找到
If no line matches, winner finds nothing,

85
00:05:36,112 --> 00:05:38,756
就返回 None，意思是“没有人”
and hands back None, which means nobody.

86
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:43,425
最巧妙的部分来了：一个叫 explore 的函数
Now for the clever part:

87
00:05:43,425 --> 00:05:45,826
explore 就是“探索”的意思
a function called explore.

88
00:05:46,146 --> 00:05:47,817
我们告诉它轮到谁
We tell it whose turn it is,

89
00:05:47,817 --> 00:05:52,645
它的任务是统计从现在这个棋盘往后，还可能出现多少局
and its job is to count every game that can still happen from the current board.

90
00:05:52,883 --> 00:05:55,247
它一开头就是两个停止条件
It starts with two stopping rules.

91
00:05:55,567 --> 00:05:58,972
如果已经有人赢了，那就是下完的一局
If someone has already won, that's one finished game,

92
00:05:58,972 --> 00:06:01,440
所以 explore 返回数字 1
so explore hands back the number 1.

93
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:06,517
如果棋盘满了却没有人赢，那就是平局，也算下完的一局
If the board is full with no winner, that's a draw, also one finished game.

94
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:08,963
否则，这一局就还没结束
Otherwise, the game isn't over yet.

95
00:06:09,283 --> 00:06:12,185
于是 explore 会试每一个空格子
So explore tries every empty square.

96
00:06:12,505 --> 00:06:16,724
它在那里放上这一方的棋子，再问自己同一个问题
It puts the player's mark there, and then asks itself the same question,

97
00:06:16,724 --> 00:06:20,577
这次轮到对方：从这里往后，还能下出多少局？
now for the other player: how many games can happen from here?

98
00:06:20,897 --> 00:06:22,638
它把所有的答案加起来
It adds up all the answers.

99
00:06:22,933 --> 00:06:26,472
我们把第一个小棋盘放大看看，这时轮到 O
Let's zoom into the first of those, with O to move.

100
00:06:26,792 --> 00:06:30,733
如果 O 下在右上角那格，O 就赢了：算 1 局
If O takes the top-right square, O wins: that's 1 game.

101
00:06:31,053 --> 00:06:33,965
擦掉它，这回试试上边中间那格
Erase it, and try the top-middle square instead.

102
00:06:34,285 --> 00:06:39,026
然后 X 填上最后一格，结果是平局：再算 1 局
Then X fills the last square, and it's a draw: 1 more.

103
00:06:39,346 --> 00:06:42,084
撤销这两步，再加起来：2 局
Undo both moves, and add up: 2 games.

104
00:06:42,404 --> 00:06:46,119
再算上另外两个分支，2 加 1 加 2 等于 5
With the other two branches, 2 plus 1 plus 2 makes 5.

105
00:06:46,367 --> 00:06:48,664
像这样，函数自己调用自己
When a function calls itself,

106
00:06:48,664 --> 00:06:52,199
也就是自己问自己同一个问题，就叫作递归
asking itself the same question like this, it's called recursive.

107
00:06:52,519 --> 00:06:54,620
听起来好像会没完没了
That might sound like it goes on forever,

108
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:59,204
但每调用一次就多一个棋子，所以总会碰到停止条件
but each call adds one more mark, so a stopping rule always kicks in.

109
00:06:59,524 --> 00:07:01,579
想象一棵倒过来的树
Picture an upside-down tree.

110
00:07:01,899 --> 00:07:06,114
空棋盘在最上面，每一种可能的走法是一个分支
The empty board is at the top, every possible move is a branch,

111
00:07:06,114 --> 00:07:08,796
而下完的每一局都是一片叶子
and every finished game is a leaf.

112
00:07:09,116 --> 00:07:12,708
我们的 explore 会沿着每一条分支往下走
Explore walks down every branch, one at a time,

113
00:07:12,708 --> 00:07:16,129
一次走一条，再数一数走到了多少片叶子
and counts the leaves it reaches.

114
00:07:16,367 --> 00:07:18,980
还有一行代码，很容易被忽略
There's one more line, and it's easy to miss.

115
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:23,460
程序下每一局都用同一个棋盘，就像只有一块白板
The program plays every game on just one board, like a single whiteboard.

116
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:27,446
所以每探索完一步，它就要擦掉那个棋子
So after exploring a move, it erases that mark.

117
00:07:27,766 --> 00:07:32,756
这叫“撤销”这一步，这样棋盘恢复原样，下一个分支就能接着试
That's called undoing the move, and it means the next branch starts fresh.

118
00:07:33,076 --> 00:07:37,028
先试走一条路，再退回来试下一条，这就叫回溯
Trying a path, then stepping back to try the next one, is called backtracking.

119
00:07:39,050 --> 00:07:42,812
想弄懂一个程序，有个好办法：故意把它改坏
A great way to understand a program is to break it on purpose.

120
00:07:43,132 --> 00:07:47,621
暂停想一想：如果删掉“撤销”那一行，你觉得会发生什么？
Pause and ponder: what do you think happens if we delete the undo line?

121
00:07:57,867 --> 00:07:59,467
程序只输出 3
The program prints just 3.

122
00:07:59,674 --> 00:08:02,311
没有了撤销，什么都不会被擦掉
Without undo, nothing ever gets erased.

123
00:08:02,631 --> 00:08:06,219
程序先下一局，按顺序一格一格地填
The program plays one game, filling the squares in order,

124
00:08:06,219 --> 00:08:09,659
直到 X 在第 7 步连成一条对角线
until X makes a diagonal on move 7.

125
00:08:09,979 --> 00:08:11,287
这是第 1 局
That's 1.

126
00:08:11,337 --> 00:08:16,219
接着它去试 X 的其他下法，可是原来那个 X 还在
Then it tries X's other choices, but the old X is still there.

127
00:08:16,539 --> 00:08:18,575
X 下在下边中间那格
X lands on the bottom-middle square,

128
00:08:18,575 --> 00:08:22,739
原来那条对角线又算赢了一次：这是第 2 局
and the old diagonal counts as a win again: that's 2.

129
00:08:23,059 --> 00:08:25,749
然后是右下角那格：第 3 局
Then the bottom-right square: that's 3.

130
00:08:26,069 --> 00:08:29,075
现在棋盘满了，再也没有可以试的了
Now the board is full, so there's nothing left to try.

131
00:08:29,317 --> 00:08:33,724
现在把“撤销”那一行放回去，改成删掉“判断输赢”
Now put undo back, and delete the winner check instead,

132
00:08:33,724 --> 00:08:36,383
这样对局要等棋盘满了才会停
so games only stop when the board is full.

133
00:08:36,703 --> 00:08:38,753
暂停一下，先猜猜答案
Pause and predict the answer.

134
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,197
362,880
362,880.

135
00:08:51,517 --> 00:08:53,117
这正是 9 的阶乘！
That's nine factorial!

136
00:08:53,170 --> 00:08:57,606
没有了判断输赢，程序在有人赢了之后还会接着下
Without the winner check, the program keeps playing after a win,

137
00:08:57,606 --> 00:09:00,692
所以它把所有幽灵对局都算进去了
so it counts all the ghost games.

138
00:09:01,012 --> 00:09:03,957
它自己又找回了我们最早算出的那个数
It rediscovered our very first count.

139
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:09,089
现在，我们把每一行都放回去，运行真正的程序
Now let's put every line back and run the real program.

140
00:09:09,409 --> 00:09:13,308
过了一小会儿，它输出了 255,168
After a moment, it prints 255,168.

141
00:09:13,550 --> 00:09:17,329
我们按对局在第几步结束，把这个总数拆开来看
Let's split that total by when each game ends.

142
00:09:17,649 --> 00:09:20,255
1,440 局在第 5 步结束
1,440 end on move 5,

143
00:09:20,255 --> 00:09:25,259
5,328 局在第 6 步结束，和我们手算的结果一样
and 5,328 on move 6, the same numbers we found by hand.

144
00:09:25,579 --> 00:09:30,316
然后柱子一下子升高了：约 4.8 万局在第 7 步结束
Then the bars shoot up: about 48 thousand end on move 7,

145
00:09:30,316 --> 00:09:32,616
7.3 万局在第 8 步结束
and 73 thousand on move 8.

146
00:09:32,936 --> 00:09:36,339
有一半多一点的对局会下满 9 步
Just over half of all games use all 9 moves:

147
00:09:36,339 --> 00:09:41,080
约 8.2 万局是 X 赢，还有 46,080 局是平局
about 82 thousand X wins, plus 46,080 draws.

148
00:09:41,401 --> 00:09:44,345
加起来就是 255,168
Together, that's 255,168.

149
00:09:44,583 --> 00:09:47,670
再来看看，这和 9 的阶乘有什么关系
And here's how it connects to nine factorial.

150
00:09:47,990 --> 00:09:52,021
还记得吗，9 的阶乘把在第 5 步结束的每一局
Remember, nine factorial counted each game that ends on move 5 a total of 24 times,

151
00:09:52,021 --> 00:09:55,209
都算了 24 次，每个幽灵对局算一次
once for each ghost ending.

152
00:09:55,529 --> 00:10:00,752
在第 6 步结束的一局被算了 6 次，在第 7 步结束的，算了两次
A game ending on move 6 was counted 6 times, and on move 7, twice.

153
00:10:01,072 --> 00:10:03,905
在第 8 步或第 9 步结束的对局
Games that end on move 8 or 9 have at most one empty square,

154
00:10:03,905 --> 00:10:07,609
最多只剩一个空格子，所以它们只算了一次
so they were counted just once.

155
00:10:07,929 --> 00:10:10,750
把每根柱子乘上各自被算的次数
Multiply each bar by its number, add them up,

156
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:13,882
再全部加起来，正好又是 9 的阶乘
and you get exactly nine factorial again.

157
00:10:16,783 --> 00:10:18,383
谁赢的对局最多？
Who wins the most games?

158
00:10:18,545 --> 00:10:23,970
X 赢了 131,184 局，O 赢了 77,904 局
X wins 131,184 of them, O wins 77,904,

159
00:10:23,970 --> 00:10:27,133
还有 46,080 局是平局
and 46,080 are draws.

160
00:10:27,453 --> 00:10:31,039
在所有可能的对局里，X 赢的超过一半
X wins in more than half of all possible games,

161
00:10:31,039 --> 00:10:33,743
因为先走让 X 有更多机会赢
because going first gives X more chances to win.

162
00:10:33,983 --> 00:10:35,355
最后一道题
One last puzzle.

163
00:10:35,405 --> 00:10:39,426
X 的第一步下在哪儿，能下出的不同对局最多
Which first move for X leads to the most different games:

164
00:10:39,426 --> 00:10:41,522
角上、边上，还是中心？
a corner, an edge, or the center?

165
00:10:41,842 --> 00:10:43,577
暂停一下，猜一猜
Pause and guess.

166
00:10:53,817 --> 00:10:56,230
没想到吧：答案是边格
Surprise:

167
00:10:56,230 --> 00:11:01,362
也就是每条边正中间的那一格，有 29,592 种对局
the edge, with 29,592 games.

168
00:11:01,682 --> 00:11:09,248
每个角格有 27,732，而中心最少，只有 25,872。为什么？
Each corner gives 27,732, and the center the fewest, just 25,872. Why?

169
00:11:09,568 --> 00:11:14,975
中心在 4 条获胜线上，角格在 3 条上，而边格只在 2 条上
The center sits on 4 winning lines, a corner on 3, and an edge on just 2.

170
00:11:15,295 --> 00:11:19,850
线越多，X 越有机会在第 5 步或第 7 步提前赢
More lines give X more chances to win early, on move 5 or 7,

171
00:11:19,850 --> 00:11:24,120
而每一次提前赢，都会从树上砍掉一大片分支
and every early win chops whole branches off the tree.

172
00:11:24,367 --> 00:11:28,213
但要小心：能下出的对局多，不代表这一步更好
But careful: more games doesn't mean a better move.

173
00:11:28,533 --> 00:11:33,258
在所有先下中心的对局里，X 每 10 局大约赢 6 局
Out of all the games that start in the center, X wins about 6 in 10.

174
00:11:33,578 --> 00:11:36,592
先下边格的话，X 赢不到一半
Starting on an edge, X wins fewer than half.

175
00:11:38,633 --> 00:11:41,710
那么，先走的 X 是不是总能赢？
So does going first mean X always wins?

176
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:45,400
不是。电脑能做的，不只是统计对局
No. A computer can do more than count.

177
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,557
它从树的最底下开始
It starts at the bottom of the tree,

178
00:11:47,557 --> 00:11:51,413
那里每一局都已经下完，然后一层一层往上推
where every game is finished, and works upward.

179
00:11:51,733 --> 00:11:55,016
每到一个分支，它都挑最好的一步
At every branch it picks the best move:

180
00:11:55,016 --> 00:12:00,062
轮到 X 时挑对 X 最好的，轮到 O 时挑对 O 最好的
best for X on X's turns, and best for O on O's turns.

181
00:12:00,382 --> 00:12:03,578
这样一来，它就把井字棋彻底算透了
Doing that, it has solved tic-tac-toe:

182
00:12:03,578 --> 00:12:06,962
如果双方都不失误，每一局都会是平局
if both players play perfectly, every game ends in a draw.

183
00:12:07,282 --> 00:12:11,581
所以 X 赢下的每一局，都少不了 O 在某一步的失误
So every one of X's wins needs a mistake by O somewhere.

184
00:12:14,016 --> 00:12:16,092
国际象棋也能这样算吗？
Could we do the same for chess?

185
00:12:16,412 --> 00:12:17,816
完全不可能
Not a chance.

186
00:12:17,866 --> 00:12:22,181
1950 年，数学家兼工程师克劳德·香农估计
In 1950, the mathematician and engineer Claude Shannon estimated

187
00:12:22,181 --> 00:12:26,847
国际象棋至少有 10 的 120 次方种可能的对局
that chess has at least 10 to the power of 120 possible games.

188
00:12:27,167 --> 00:12:29,676
那可是 1 后面跟着 120 个零！
That's a 1 followed by 120 zeros!

189
00:12:29,996 --> 00:12:34,643
而我们能观测到的整个宇宙，也只有大约 10 的 80 次方个原子
The whole observable universe has only about 10 to the power of 80 atoms.

190
00:12:34,883 --> 00:12:38,691
所以，国际象棋程序没法探索每一个分支
So chess programs can't explore every branch.

191
00:12:39,011 --> 00:12:42,778
它们只往后看几步，再估计谁更有希望赢
They look only so many moves ahead, then estimate who's winning,

192
00:12:42,778 --> 00:12:46,147
靠的是从几百万局练习中学到的经验
using what they learned from millions of practice games.

193
00:12:46,467 --> 00:12:49,171
但说到底，思路和你刚学的一样
But underneath, it's the same idea you just learned:

194
00:12:49,171 --> 00:12:52,956
把走法排成一棵树，一个分支一个分支地探索
a tree of moves, explored one branch at a time.

195
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:54,917
我们来小结一下
Let's recap.

196
00:12:54,967 --> 00:12:57,432
把每一步的选择数乘起来
Multiplying the choices gives nine factorial, 362,880 orders.

197
00:12:57,432 --> 00:13:01,458
就得到 9 的阶乘，一共 362,880 种顺序
Multiplying the choices gives nine factorial, 362,880 orders.

198
00:13:01,778 --> 00:13:04,455
但只要有人赢，对局就会停下
But games stop when someone wins,

199
00:13:04,455 --> 00:13:07,704
所以这些顺序里有很多都是幽灵对局
so many of those orders are ghost games.

200
00:13:08,024 --> 00:13:12,287
而一段短短的递归程序，先试走一步，往下探索
And a short recursive program counts every real game by trying a move,

201
00:13:12,287 --> 00:13:16,162
再撤销，就把每一局真实对局都统计了一遍
exploring, and undoing it.

202
00:13:16,482 --> 00:13:19,517
答案正好是 255,168
The answer is exactly 255,168.

203
00:13:19,766 --> 00:13:21,366
现在，轮到你了
Now it's your turn.

204
00:13:21,566 --> 00:13:25,126
改一改程序，让它只统计 X 赢的对局
Change the program so it counts only the games X wins,

205
00:13:25,126 --> 00:13:31,034
或者只统计在第 7 步结束的对局，或者看看如果 O 先走会怎样
or only the games that end on move 7, or see what happens if O goes first.

206
00:13:31,354 --> 00:13:34,592
程序和挑战题的链接都在视频简介里
The program and the challenges are linked in the description.

207
00:13:34,912 --> 00:13:36,512
动手去探索吧！
Have fun exploring!
